invariant: INV-14
file: srv.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_widemul
reason: srv_config_ok stops asking for the caller's answer about the widening
  multiply, so every server init call takes a configuration that never
  stated it. ch_srv_check keeps its own rule, so the init rows notice:
  test/tcp_nonblocking_loop_widemul.h requires ch_srv_record_init to
  refuse 0 and 3 with CH_EINVAL and a failed session.

--- old
#ifdef CH_WIDEMUL_RUNTIME
    // The caller's answer about the widening multiply (cpu_cfg.h).
    if (!widemul_answer_ok(cfg)) {
        return 0;
    }
#endif
    return srv_fields_ok(cfg)
--- new
    return srv_fields_ok(cfg)
